# CHAIN-LINK corpus · AXIS = the kind of postfix link sitting between the two
# method calls of a chain. CELL SAMPLED HERE: the link is an EMethodCall (the
# ADJACENT-receiver cell) over a USER-DEFINED (non-builtin) receiver type.
#
# `parse_expr_bp_with_lhs` (which binds `int bp_start = lhs.span.start`) and
# `parse_dot_expr` (which binds `int start = lhs.span.start`) give every link of
# a postfix spine the same `span.start`, so the span.start-keyed `expr_types`
# table is a CONTENDED slot.
# The outer link's own type is published only on `expr_link_types[span.end]`,
# and only by `infer_expr_type`. When the typechecker's targ-recorder skips
# that call for the outer link, the lowerer falls back to the contended slot
# and mints the outer link's destination with its RECEIVER's type -- the
# emitted C then does not compile.
#
# Sibling cells: chain_link_field / chain_link_field_nested (EFieldAccess),
# chain_link_index / chain_link_index_nested (EIndex),
# chain_link_propagate (EPropagate), chain_link_builtin_recv_control (builtin
# receiver, the accidentally-green control).
from std.heap import Heap

void main():
    Heap[int] empty = Heap[int].new()
    print(empty.pop().is_none())
    print(empty.pop().is_some())
    Heap[int] full = Heap[int].new()
    full.push(7)
    print(full.pop().is_some())
    print(full.pop().is_none())
